  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Russia Food Price Crisis Rapid Response Trust Fund for Tajikistan and Kyrgyz Republic</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;THIS TRUST FUND COMPLEMENTS THE ACTIVITIES UNDERTAKEN UNDER THE BA  USD1.2 billion food facility (This includes IBRD and IDA funds as well  as the single-donor TF approved from IBRD Surplus)approved by the  Board of EDs to allow fast track activities in support of countries&apos;  response to the food crisis, and the Food Price Crisis Response Core  MDTF; in particular it allows targeted aid from Russia to Tajikistan  and the Kyrgyz Republic&quot;&quot;
 
 Program Objectives: (see also the Global Food Crisis Response Program  Framework Document for more detailed Program description)
 1. Reduce the negative impact of high food prices on the lives of the  poor in a timely manner
 2. Support the Tajik and Kyrgyz governments in the design of  sustainable policies that mitigate the adverse impacts of more  volatile food prices on poverty
 3. Support broad-based growth in productivity and market participation  in agriculture to ensure an adequate supply response as part of a  sustained improvement in food supply.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
